-- title:
--   Completion of a node ring is O[[U,V]]/(UV-varpi)
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, and let $\varpi \in O$ be irreducible (a uniformiser). Let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring equipped with an $O$-algebra structure, and let $x, y \in R$ satisfy: $xy$ equals the image of $\varpi$ under the structure map $O \to R$; the maximal ideal of $R$ is the ideal generated by $x$ and $y$; the composite of $O \to R$ with the residue map of $R$ is surjective, i.e. $O$ surjects onto the residue field of $R$; and the Krull dimension of $R$ is at least $2$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak m_R$-adic completion of $R$ onto the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $O[[X_0,X_1]]$ (formal power series indexed by `Fin 2`) by the principal ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \varpi$, such that: for every $o \in O$, $\iota$ carries the image in the completion of the element $o \cdot 1 \in R$ to the class of the constant series $o$; $\iota$ carries the image of $x$ to the class $U$ of $X_0$; and $\iota$ carries the image of $y$ to the class $V$ of $X_1$. Thus $\iota$ is an isomorphism of rings which is automatically $O$-equivariant by its first property.
--
--   This is the local structure theorem at an ordinary double point (node): a two-dimensional Noetherian local $O$-algebra whose maximal ideal is generated by two elements with product a uniformiser has completion the standard crossing model $O[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi)$, with the given generators corresponding to the two branch coordinates $U$ and $V$. It feeds the identification of the complete local ring at a crossing point in the integral model used later, being cited by [`IsLocalRing.nonempty_algEquiv_uvCrossingModel_of_mul_eq_of_maximalIdeal_eq_sup_span_pair_sup_sq_of_two_le_ringKrullDim`](thm.html#IsLocalRing.nonempty_algEquiv_uvCrossingModel_of_mul_eq_of_maximalIdeal_eq_sup_span_pair_sup_sq_of_two_le_ringKrullDim).
